  "text": "In Donoghue v Stevenson [1932] UKHL 100, the House of Lords established the modern doctrine of negligence. The claimant, Mrs May Donoghue, sought damages of £500 against the manufacturer. Lord Atkin delivered the leading judgment on 26 May 1932, articulating the 'neighbour principle' that remains binding authority across common-law jurisdictions.",
