  "text": "Under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, the dishonour of a cheque constitutes a criminal offence in India. The Supreme Court of India, in Dashrath Rupsingh Rathod v State of Maharashtra (2014), clarified the territorial jurisdiction for such complaints, holding that the case must be filed where the drawee bank is situated.",
  "id": 220,
  "label": [
    {
      "start": 6,
      "end": 57,
      "text": "Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881",
      "labels": [
